      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14202290/assets/815e7943ff4f01bf9a89cd6bb1214cf9266c8ae528cfd53e05a7ac56cf1e0e74.png)\n\nThe graph above shows a direct variation between the variables $y$ and $x.$ Which equation describes the relationship between the variables?",
      "worked_solution": "Since $y$ varies directly with $x,$ we use the equation\n\n$$\ny=kx.\n$$\n\nNext, we notice there is a point on the graph with $y=8$ and $x=2.$ So, we substitute this data into the equation to find $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8 & =k\\cdot 2 \\\\ \\frac{8}{2} & =k \\\\ 4 & =k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the direct variation equation is given by\n\n$$\ny=4x.\n$$",
